.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt WATTLE-PROJECTS 7
.Os Wattle DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-projects
.Nd how Wattle projects, libraries and dependencies are laid out
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A project is a directory containing an
.Ar info file ,
source files (in either Wattle or Zig)
and documentation.
.Xr wattle-build 1
builds the exes and libs that a project declares,
.Xr wattle-deps 1
manages the dependencies of a project and
.Xr wattle-test 1
runs its tests.
This page describes what a project contains.
.Pp
A project may include one or more
.Ar applications ,
installable by
.Xr wattle-apps 1 .
For more information on this,
see
.Xr wattle-applications 7 .
A project that other projects use is a
.Ar library .
See
.Sx "LIBRARIES" .
.
.Sh LAYOUT
A project has an
.Ql "info\&.edn"
at its root.
This is the
.Ar info file .
Every other file is optional.
.
.Sh INFO FILE
The info file holds one map.
All keys are optional,
but
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":group"
are needed to install a project as an application:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":name"
.Xc
The name of the project.
It is one directory name and is unique across groups.
.It Xo
.Ql ":group"
.Xc
The group of the project,
by convention a reverse domain such as
.Ql "org\&.example" .
The value is used in a directory name and so cannot be empty,
.Ql "\&."
or
.Ql "\&.\&." .
It cannot contain a path separator.
.It Xo
.Ql ":vendored"
.Xc
A vector of maps that describe the sources that
.Ql "wattle deps vendor"
copies into the project.
Each has a
.Ql ":name"
and a
.Ql ":url" ,
and may have a
.Ql ":ref" ,
a
.Ql ":prefix"
and
.Ql ":paths" .
See
.Sx "VENDORING"
and
.Xr wattle-deps 1 .
.It Xo
.Ql ":exes"
.Xc
A vector of maps that describe the programs of the project.
Each has a
.Ql ":type" ,
.Ql ":native" ,
.Ql ":source"
or
.Ql ":web" ,
a
.Ql ":name"
and an
.Ql ":entry" .
See ‘Declarations’ in
.Xr wattle-build 1 .
.It Xo
.Ql ":libs"
.Xc
A vector of maps that describe the libraries of the project.
Each has a
.Ql ":type" ,
.Ql ":native" ,
.Ql ":source"
or
.Ql ":remote" ,
a
.Ql ":name"
and may have
.Ql ":for" ,
the names of the exes it is part of.
See
.Sx "LIBRARIES" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":docs"
.Xc
A vector of maps that describe the documentation of the project.
Each has a
.Ql ":type" ,
.Ql ":man"
or
.Ql ":web" ,
.Ql ":files"
and may have
.Ql ":for" ,
the names of the exes it is part of.
A
.Ql ":man"
doc’s section is the digit that ends each file name,
so
.Ql "man/greet\&.1"
is in section 1.
.El
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{:name \(dqgreeter\(dq
 :group \(dqorg\&.example\(dq
 :vendored \(lB{:name \(dqgreetings\(dq
             :url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/greetings\&.git\(dq
             :prefix \(dqdeps/greetings\(dq}\(rB
 :exes \(lB{:type :native
         :name \(dqhello\(dq
         :entry \(dqmain\&.wattle\(dq}\(rB
 :libs \(lB{:type :source
         :name \(dqutil\(dq
         :files \(lB\(dqutil/\(dq\(rB
         :for \(lB\(dqhello\(dq\(rB}\(rB
 :docs \(lB{:type :man
         :files \(lB\(dqman/hello\&.1\(dq\(rB
         :for \(lB\(dqhello\(dq\(rB}\(rB}
.Ed
.
.Sh LIBRARIES
A library is code that a project uses and does not run by itself.
A project declares the libraries it imports by name in
.Ql ":libs"
in its info file,
and
.Ql "wattle build lib"
places each on the module path.
A bare import,
as in
.Ql "\*(lpimport greet\*(rp" ,
finds a library by its
.Ql ":name" .
See ‘MODULES’ in
.Xr wattle 7 .
.Pp
There are three kinds of declaration:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":source"
.Xc
Wattle source files in the project.
.Ql "wattle build lib"
copies its
.Ql ":files"
to
.Ql "\&.wattle/<name>/" ,
where each keeps its path.
.It Xo
.Ql ":native"
.Xc
A native module,
built from its Zig
.Ql ":root"
file in
.Ql "zig-out/lib" .
A native executable whose name the
.Ql ":for"
of the library holds links it.
.It Xo
.Ql ":remote"
.Xc
A library in another project,
fetched from
.Ql ":url"
at a pinned
.Ql ":ref"
or
.Ql ":hash" .
Its own info file declares it as
.Ql ":source"
or
.Ql ":native" ,
and it is placed as that form.
.El
.Pp
.Ql "\&.wattle"
holds material that is not committed.
.Ql "wattle build lib"
creates it with a
.Ql "\&.gitignore"
that excludes its contents.
.Pp
.Ql "wattle apps install"
installs a library only as part of an exe whose name its
.Ql ":for"
holds.
A library with no
.Ql ":for"
is not installed.
See
.Xr wattle-applications 7 .
.
.Sh VENDORING
Vendoring a dependency refers to the practice of copying into
the source tree of a project the Wattle source files that the
project uses.
A vendored dependency is not on the module path.
Within the code,
it is imported using a relative import:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*(lpimport \&./deps/greetings\*(rp
.Ed
.Pp
A vendored copy is the version the project was tested with,
it changes only when the project’s author changes it and the
project runs without any dependency being fetched.
A project includes a copy of each dependency and a fix to a
dependency reaches the project only when its author updates the
copy.
.Pp
A
.Ql ":remote"
library is the alternative.
The project names the source and pins a revision of it,
and the copy is fetched into
.Ql "\&.wattle"
and is not committed.
.Ql ":for"
does not affect vendoring:
any library of another project may be vendored.
.Pp
The project lists what it vendors under
.Ql ":vendored"
in its info file,
and
.Ql "wattle deps vendor"
copies each entry into the project.
See
.Xr wattle-deps 1 .
An entry without a
.Ql ":ref"
uses the HEAD of the default branch of a Git repository each
time.
The copies belong to the project and may be edited,
and no record is kept of the revision they came from.
.
